<id/13/1349/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Scammony"@en ;
    skos:broadMatch <customs-1866/plant_root/#concept> ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_drugs_medicinal_botanicals/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "a entharctic gum-resin from the root of *Convolvulus Scammonia*, which is seldom to be obtained pure, being largely adulterated with chalk. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 343]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated classification (group=grp_drugs_medicinal_botanicals): Named materia medica (castoreum, ginseng, cubebs, scammony, maidenhair, liquorice juice, quassia, cocculus indicus, serpentary, asafoetida, cantharides, hellebore, pipsissewa, ipecacuanha) left in the residual bin. Layer-1 observations: 13 rows, 1856–1866. Series: HCPP_Annual Statement of Trade ×13. Units: Lbs. (Pounds) ×13. Top routes: World → United Kingdom ×3; Other Parts → United Kingdom ×3; Turkey Proper → United Kingdom ×3; Syria and Palestine → United Kingdom ×3."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <id/scheme/#resource> ;
    skos:notation "1349" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Scammony"@en ;
